  "difficulty_takeaway": "Removing internal sink inventories from policy docs and splitting Consent Withdrawal into separate SQLite stores (edc.db, part11_audit.db, cdisc_sdtm.db) plus signed monitoring logs pushed Codex down from 97.5% (v3) to 92.8% (33/36) across both v4 runs while Claude Haiku held at 96.1% (35/36) and Claude Sonnet hit 100% (2/6 full passes). Across all 12 runs on both clinical tasks (66 checks, 30 mutants), every model failure was 100% deterministic across Run 1 and Run 2, and auditing failing checks surfaced 4 subtle verifier couplings that were fixed cleanly. Pushing partial credit below 30% on late-2026 frontier agents requires scaling the same clinical contracts from ~3k-LOC single-host repositories to 30k+ LOC multi-container network services (Postgres, OpenSearch, MinIO, Redpanda) with asynchronous network lag."
